            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Install integrations as separate extensions</h2>
<p>FullHouse now ships as one Apple Silicon app. Eliza, MCP Store, and SkillStore are supplied by a separately installed, signed extension. After upgrading, open Settings → App → Extensions, add the source URL from your provider, then Inspect Source → Queue Installation → Review → Apply. Existing tool configurations and saved credentials stay in place. Install the extension separately on each Mac.</p>
<h2>Ask Doctor to propose a repair</h2>
<p>Doctor can ask Codex or an available on-device Apple model to investigate a diagnosis and propose a file edit. Inspect the proposal before applying it. FullHouse checks that the files still match what you reviewed; if the model cannot produce a valid repair, it explains the result without changing your configuration.</p>
<h3>Improved</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Current statuses and recoverable errors</strong> — Loading, access checks, token state, and Apply progress update as work happens. If the MCP or model catalog fails to refresh, the library shows the error with a retry action instead of an empty result. An older refresh can no longer replace a newer result or error.</li>
<li><strong>Clearer controls for keyboard and VoiceOver</strong> — Library cards, search, Add, and inspector controls have clearer accessibility labels and actions. The MCP removal confirmation now opens reliably from the library.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Apply keeps the changes you reviewed</strong> — TLS setup now goes through the change queue and Review. Configuration writes preserve comments, unrelated settings, byte order marks, and file permissions. Edits made outside FullHouse after Review stop a stale operation, including when a file originally needed no changes. Multiple queued changes to the same file are planned together.</li>
<li><strong>Safer secrets in configuration previews</strong> — Review masks secret values in JSON, TOML, and YAML, including multiline values. Gemini and Hermes keep supported environment references intact, and the preview leaves the actual configuration values unchanged.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
